# deploy/vps/tor/torrc-web — /etc/tor/instances/velesweb/torrc (setup.sh).
#
# Other people's fetches (PLAN-challenge-relay.md D5): the gateway's
# web_extract for a session that is not the owner's goes through this
# SOCKS port (`[web] others_proxy`), each session under a user name of
# its own, so IsolateSOCKSAuth gives each one a circuit of its own.
#
# On the WireGuard address, like the signer's API: the gateway's
# container cannot reach this host's loopback. veles.nft lets the
# gateway user connect and refuses everyone on wg0, so the other nodes
# cannot use it. An instance of its own, so a bind that fails (wg0 not up
# yet; tor-web.conf restarts it) never takes the sandboxes' TransPort
# down with it.
SocksPort 10.0.30.1:9050 IsolateSOCKSAuth
ClientOnly 1
AvoidDiskWrites 1
